# Shop Awnings and Transparent Bakery Windows

Status: DONE
Milestone: M15 Original storefront canopy and layered entrance interior
Dependencies: 19_LIGHTER_PINK_TABS_AND_MATERIAL_STUDY.todo; original entrance safety

## Purpose

Add a real shop-style striped/scalloped canopy in a suitable top position and
transparent entrance windows revealing a cute illustrated bakery interior.
The reference images inspire construction/mood only, not copied artwork.

## Tasks

- [x] Choose canopy placement beneath the normal site header and above entrance doors.
- [x] Implement a separate entrance-shop.css with true transparent glass apertures.
- [x] Add three separately moving room layers behind the doors, using the existing
  bounded pointer coordinates and distinct depth factors.
- [x] Finish original awning/backwall/shelves/counter SVGs and verify safe assets.
- [x] Verify real room pixels are visible through closed windows, not duplicate
  pictures drawn on opaque panes.
- [x] Check desktop/mobile/short-screen bounds, skip/click/keyboard and audio policy.
- [x] Review combined15tile sheet(s) within remaining two of the current three-view budget.
- [x] Refresh the six README showcase exports to match the new roof/tabs/light covers.
- [x] Publish only reviewed production files; isolated cream demo remains local.

## Acceptance criteria

- The canopy frames the top without covering navigation or hero reading.
- Windows have translucent glaze and reveal one continuous room behind both doors.
- Background, fittings and counter move at distinct restrained depths on fine pointers.
- Room art is original decorative fiction, not a claim of a real storefront/menu.
- Existing paired doors/bell/skip and no-JS/reduced-motion/direct-link safety remain.
- No cream effect is restored to the live website.

